# Both images build from the project root, so without this file the whole
# working copy — Git history, build output, local secrets — is handed to the
# Docker daemon on every build.
#
# Deny everything, then admit the packages the Dockerfiles copy. A new package
# is invisible to a build until it is listed here, which is the failure mode
# worth having: loud at build time rather than silently shipped.
**

!dartway_example_client/
!dartway_example_client/**
!dartway_example_flutter/
!dartway_example_flutter/**
!dartway_example_server/
!dartway_example_server/**

**/.dart_tool/
**/build/
**/.fvm/
**/ephemeral/
# custom_lint.log alone reaches hundreds of megabytes when the analyzer trips.
**/*.log

# Runtime secrets never travel in a build context: a credential baked into an
# image layer is a credential in every copy of that image. The deployment
# mounts this file from outside the checkout instead.
**/config/passwords.yaml
